  "summary": "An air-cooled heat exchanger (fin-fan cooler) cools or condenses a process fluid using ambient air instead of water. The fluid flows through finned tubes between header boxes; axial fans blow (forced draft) or pull (induced draft) air across the bundle. It saves cooling water and is common in refineries and gas plants.",
